// =============================================================================
// S-CODE SAMPLE - MINIMAL PROGRAM
// =============================================================================
// What it does:
//   Calls a multiplication function and stores 6 x 7 in a global variable.
// Expected result:
//   The program halts with `answer = 42` in RAM and 42 in the accumulator.
// Runs on:
//   Desktop/CLI simulators and all S-CPU hardware implementations.
// Demonstrates:
//   A function, parameters, arithmetic, a global variable, and top-level return.
// =============================================================================

// Parameters are local to the function; `return` sends the result to its caller.
int Multiply(int left, int right) {
  return left * right;
}

// Top-level statements form the program body. Global variables live in RAM.
int answer = Multiply(6, 7);

// A top-level return leaves its value in the accumulator, then halts the program.
return answer;
